Florian Engel is a classic car  enthusiast  he's taking something really special out  of his garage and the Bavarian town of  one siedel nearby white  it's a 1973 Corolla Levine Toyota  introduced a second version of the  Corolla in Japan in 1970 a year later  the Corolla was marketed in Germany and  sold 20,000 models it was yet another  success for the Japanese car industry  abroad but the Levine model which is  like the GTI of Corollas was only  available for customers in Japan and the  US  Florian ENGOs Levine is probably the  only one in Germany or even Europe he  found it on an American car forum and  convinced the owner to sell him the rare  model even though the car is a decade  older than its owner the Levine's  4-cylinder 1.6 liter engine still powers  it up to 108 horsepower and a top speed  of 183 on the Autobahn the Corollas line  seemed a bit odd yet somehow familiar  it's a typical compact car with European  dimensions some say the design is  reminiscent of the Ford Escort others  say it's more like an Opel cadet a few  of the details are a bit too quirky  Florian says when he takes the car to  old timer events few people recognize it  as a Toyota there's little to reveal  what it is except for the old Toyota  badge on the grille it says Corolla on  the side that's when people realise what  it is the Corolla was supposed to  conquer new markets for Toyota  some say that explains its aesthetic the  curvy fastback rear end is reminiscent  of American muscle cars downscaled just  slightly a full family of Corolla models  were made a sedan station wagon and a  sporty two-door known to insiders as te  27 florian says that when he looks at  the TE 27 he sees that its design has  been influenced by a wide range of cars  it's like that with most Japanese autos  he says the thing that makes it special  is that it's a mix of all types of  styles and as a result has created  something new it's not like Italian cars  that always originate their own lines  but a combination is it coming off the  oil the interior by contrast is quite  Spartan there are a few sporty  accessories like a rev counter which was  a contemporary feature there's lots of  plastic with a hint of chrome nothing  flashy to distract from the driving  experience  the advantage of the sparse interior  trim what's not there  can't break florian says that you really  have to be passionate about Japanese  cars because getting spare parts for  them takes patience there are still  parts in Japan and the American market  for them is big but fluorine says in  Germany it's difficult to get parts here  when something breaks tight it's a clean  venomous couple toes thank goodness  there's very little that breaks when it  comes to large series classics that are  made in Japan the Corolla Levine is  robust Florian can simply focus on the  joy of driving it Lavie means lightning  bolt and refers to the cars driving  performance the little car from Japan  doesn't have to hide its light under a  stone it weighs 850 kilograms and goes  from 0 to 100 kilometers an hour in 9  seconds the chassis technology is solid  rigid axle suspended with leaf springs  were standard in compact car  construction in the 1970s  the Corolla showpiece is under the hood  to double barrel carburetors ensure that  the dual overhead cam straight  4-cylinder 1.6 liter engine purrs with  power modeled on Alfa Romeos of the time  motorcycle manufacturer Yamaha supported  Toyota and developing the cylinder head  the growl lets everyone know the Corolla  isn't just cute Florian became a Toyota  fan early on his grandfather founded one  of the first Toyota outlets in Germany  in 1975 Florian's dad and uncle  Friedhelm  later took over the company in the 1980s  in addition to selling maintaining and  repairing current Toyota models Toyota  specialist Friedhelm Engel has got a  side job he restores classic cars  most of them vintage Toyotas this green  silica is about finished it's being  completely rebuilt for his own  collection  if Florian has a problem or can't get  apart  uncle fleet home always has a solution  the area around home has plenty of  sinuous roads making it perfect driving  territory for Florian angle in his  levine he loves going out for rides in  his rare vehicle  and there's one thing the Toyota fan can  be certain of it's not likely he'll run  into someone with a car like his anytime  soon
 

